Based on my search through all Slack channels, **Alice** made the first public declaration of resistance to the migration in the **#engineering** channel.

Specifically, on **November 10, 2024 at 12:00:00**, Alice posted:

> "I'm done. I will not migrate our Python codebase to legacy Java infrastructure just to satisfy some corporate checkbox. This is technical vandalism. Looking at other opportunities."

This was the first explicit statement of resistance to the migration in any public channel. Prior to this, there had been concerns and pushback expressed by various team members (Bob and Diana questioned the feasibility and technical merits), but Alice's message on November 10th was the first definitive public declaration of refusal to comply with the migration requirements.
